WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.800
What does this error mean, and how do I figure it out on

2
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.270
my own? In this mission, you break a function on purpose.

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:07.320
Look at this code.

4
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.620
It asks for a field called nome,

5
00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:12.660
which means name. Now write this down:

6
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.700
what happens if it gets an empty event?

7
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.070
And what status code do you expect?

8
00:00:17.453 --> 00:00:20.643
Download the mission's two files and run this command.

9
00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:23.693
You only need Python, no AWS account.

10
00:00:23.693 --> 00:00:25.313
An error shows up:

11
00:00:25.313 --> 00:00:27.663
KeyError, and the name of the field.

12
00:00:27.833 --> 00:00:30.173
In other words, the code looked for the field called nome,

13
00:00:30.173 --> 00:00:31.623
and it wasn't there.

14
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:33.850
Now use AI as a tutor.

15
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.690
Paste this request, with the code and the error.

16
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.490
Notice: you ask it not to give you the fix.

17
00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.970
It points to the line and asks you a question.

18
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.440
Once you understand the cause,

19
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.160
fix it yourself. What should the function do when the name

20
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:46.750
is missing?

21
00:00:47.153 --> 00:00:48.453
If you already have an account,

22
00:00:48.453 --> 00:00:50.533
create the function on AWS.

23
00:00:50.533 --> 00:00:52.293
The commands are in the mission.

24
00:00:52.293 --> 00:00:54.313
Then call it with an empty event.

25
00:00:54.313 --> 00:00:56.513
This was the real response in our test.

26
00:00:56.513 --> 00:00:57.793
Look at the detail.

27
00:00:57.793 --> 00:01:00.653
StatusCode 200. Right next to it:

28
00:01:00.653 --> 00:01:02.313
FunctionError, Unhandled.

29
00:01:02.313 --> 00:01:04.563
And inside the file: KeyError.

30
00:01:04.953 --> 00:01:06.523
That's the point of this mission.

31
00:01:06.793 --> 00:01:10.263
The status is 200, and the function still failed.

32
00:01:10.753 --> 00:01:14.223
The 200 says the call to the Lambda service worked.

33
00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:17.263
Your function's error is in FunctionError.

34
00:01:17.453 --> 00:01:18.813
If you only look at the status,

35
00:01:18.813 --> 00:01:20.263
you think everything went fine.

36
00:01:20.653 --> 00:01:23.253
Wait about 15 seconds and read the log.

37
00:01:23.253 --> 00:01:25.483
It shows the error and line 5.

38
00:01:25.673 --> 00:01:28.403
Now ask your AI, without showing it this mission:

39
00:01:28.713 --> 00:01:30.673
if the StatusCode came back 200,

40
00:01:30.673 --> 00:01:33.383
did my function run without errors?

41
00:01:33.553 --> 00:01:34.883
Ask for the documentation.

42
00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:36.523
Did it notice the difference?

43
00:01:36.593 --> 00:01:37.863
Does the link confirm it?

44
00:01:38.313 --> 00:01:39.443
Open it and write it down.

45
00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:41.170
At the end, clean up.

46
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.980
The mission has the commands to delete the function,

47
00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:45.430
the role and the log group.

48
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.630
The last line has to show empty brackets.

49
00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:49.850
That means the function is off the list.

50
00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.610
Then write your article:

51
00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.710
my Lambda returned 200 and it was broken.

52
00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.130
AI only reviews.

53
